## How to avoid phone snatchers on the street

Most snatches in London happen in a few seconds, often by two people on an e-bike riding on the pavement, or by groups working together near busy stations. A few habits make you a much harder target:

- **Look up and around before you take your phone out**, especially near the kerb, at crossings and outside stations.
- **Stand with your back to a wall** when you use your phone in the street, not at the edge of the pavement.
- **Hold your phone with both hands**, or step into a shop to use it.
- **Use your fingerprint or face to unlock in public**, so nobody can watch you type your PIN.
- **Keep it in a zipped inside pocket or bag** when you're not using it, not in a back pocket or on a café table.
- **Watch out for two people on one e-bike or moped.** Police say riding "two up" is a common sign of snatchers.

## How to be ready before it happens

Most of the steps above work much better if you prepare in advance. It takes 10 minutes:

- **Save your IMEI.** Dial `*#06#` and save the number somewhere other than your phone, like your email.
- **Turn on Remote Lock and Find Hub**, so you can lock and locate your phone from any device.
- **Turn on Theft Detection Lock**, which locks your phone automatically if it's snatched from your hand.
- **Turn on Identity Check.** Away from places you trust, it asks for your fingerprint or face before anyone can change your screen lock, turn off Find Hub or reset the phone. So even a thief who saw your PIN can't switch off your protection. You'll find it under *Settings > Google > All services > Theft protection* on phones that support it.
- **Hide message previews on your lock screen**, so thieves can't read your security codes.
- **Register your phone on Immobilise.**
- **Install CrookCatcher**, so you get a photo and the location of anyone who tries to unlock your phone.

For step-by-step instructions, read our guides to the [top 5 Android settings to secure your phone against theft](/blog/top_five_settings) and [how to stop thieves from turning off your phone](/blog/block-power-menu).

